%I A398934 #20 Aug 30 2026 23:15:02
%S A398934 1,25,675,8575,60025
%N A398934 Least positive integer that, for every k with 1 <= k <= n, is the volume of a k-dimensional rectangular box with lattice-point vertices, integral edge lengths, and every edge having nonzero components in all k coordinate directions.
%C A398934 After translating one vertex to the origin, such a k-dimensional rectangular box is determined by k pairwise perpendicular vectors v_1,...,v_k in Z^k. Every coordinate of every v_r is required to be nonzero, so each edge has a component in every coordinate direction. The length |v_r| is also required to be an integer.
%C A398934 Each edge vector v = (x_1,...,x_k) may also be viewed as the body diagonal of an axis-parallel integer-sided k-dimensional rectangular box with side lengths |x_1|,...,|x_k|. Thus every edge crosses all k coordinate directions.
%C A398934 For k=2 these are diagonal lattice rectangles in the terminology of A338886, with the additional requirement that both side lengths are integers. Their integer side lengths are hypotenuse numbers A009003.
%C A398934 The sequence is nondecreasing.
%F A398934 Let B_k = {|det(M)| : M is a k X k integer matrix with no zero entries and Transpose(M)*M = diag(d_1^2,...,d_k^2) for some positive integers d_1,...,d_k}. Then a(n) = min Intersection_{k=1..n} B_k.
%e A398934 For n=2, the vectors (3,4) and (-4,3) are perpendicular and both have length 5, giving a(2) = 25.
%e A398934 For n=3, 675 is admissible in dimension 2 using vectors (9,12) and (-36,27), of lengths 15 and 45. In dimension 3 the pairwise perpendicular vectors (1,2,2), (14,-2,-5), (-2,11,-10) have lengths 3, 15, and 15, giving volume 675. Hence a(3) = 675.
%e A398934 For n=4, 8575 is admissible in dimension 2 using vectors (1029,1372) and (-4,3), of lengths 1715 and 5. In dimension 3, the pairwise perpendicular vectors (50,75,150), (3,-6,2), (6,2,-3) have lengths 175, 7, and 7, giving volume 8575. In dimension 4 the pairwise perpendicular vectors (1,2,2,4), (2,2,5,-4), (4,4,-4,-1), (26,-23,2,4) have lengths 5, 7, 7, and 35, giving volume 8575. Hence a(4) = 8575.
%Y A398934 Cf. A338886 (diagonal lattice rectangles), A009003 (hypotenuse numbers), A327269, A327272 (integer matrices with orthogonal rows).
%K A398934 nonn,more,new
%O A398934 1,2
%A A398934 _Mike Sheppard_, Aug 14 2026
